{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/mole-concept/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/mole-concept.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Mole Concept & Stoichiometry | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-teal-400 to-cyan-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -calculator text-teal-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>The Mole Concept &amp; Stoichiometry\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding moles, molar mass, Avogadro's number, and stoichiometric calculations.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-teal-50 border-l-4 border-teal-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-teal-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define the mole and state Avogadro's number</li>\n          <li>• Calculate molar mass of elements and compounds</li>\n          <li>• Convert between moles, mass, and number of particles</li>\n          <li>• Apply stoichiometry to calculate reacting masses</li>\n          <li>• Calculate percentage composition and empirical formulae</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is a Mole? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is a Mole?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong class=\"text-teal-600\">mole</strong> is the SI unit for amount of substance. Just as we count eggs in dozens (12) or paper in reams (500), chemists count particles in moles.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-teal-100 to-cyan-100 p-6 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-800 mb-2\">One mole contains exactly:</p>\n            <p class=\"text-4xl font-bold text-teal-700 mb-2\">6.02 × 10²³</p>\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-800\">particles (atoms, molecules, ions, or electrons)</p>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2\">This number is called <strong>Avogadro's constant</strong> (L or N<sub>A</sub>)</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Why 6.02 × 10²³?</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">This number was chosen so that one mole of any element has a mass in grams equal to its relative atomic mass. For example:</p>\n          <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mt-2 space-y-1\">\n            <li>• 1 mole of carbon-12 atoms = 12 g</li>\n            <li>• 1 mole of hydrogen atoms ≈ 1 g</li>\n            <li>• 1 mole of oxygen atoms ≈ 16 g</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Molar Mass -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Molar Mass\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong class=\"text-teal-600\">molar mass</strong> (M) is the mass of one mole of a substance, expressed in grams per mole (g/mol).</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -atom mr-2\" data-mi=\"atom\">atom</span>Elements</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Molar mass = Relative atomic mass (Aᵣ) in g/mol</p>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <p>M(Na) = 23 g/mol</p>\n                <p>M(C) = 12 g/mol</p>\n                <p>M(Ca) = 40 g/mol</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Compounds</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Molar mass = Sum of atomic masses</p>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <p>M(H₂O) = (2×1) + 16 = 18 g/mol</p>\n                <p>M(NaCl) = 23 + 35.5 = 58.5 g/mol</p>\n                <p>M(H₂SO₄) = 2+32+64 = 98 g/mol</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: The Mole Triangle -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          The Mole Triangle\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-white p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center mb-4\">\n            <svg viewBox=\"0 0 300 240\" class=\"max-w-xs mx-auto\">\n              <!-- Triangle -->\n              <polygon points=\"150,20 280,200 20,200\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0d9488\" stroke-width=\"3\"></polygon>\n              \n              <!-- Mass at top -->\n              <text x=\"150\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0d9488\">Mass (m)</text>\n              <text x=\"150\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#666\">grams</text>\n              \n              <!-- Moles at bottom left -->\n              <text x=\"70\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0d9488\">Moles (n)</text>\n              <text x=\"70\" y=\"198\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#666\">mol</text>\n              \n              <!-- Molar Mass at bottom right -->\n              <text x=\"230\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0d9488\">Molar Mass</text>\n              <text x=\"230\" y=\"198\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0d9488\">(M)</text>\n              \n              <!-- Operators -->\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#666\">÷</text>\n              <text x=\"200\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#666\">×</text>\n            </svg>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-center\">\n            <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n              <p class=\"font-mono text-lg text-teal-700\">n = m/M</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">moles = mass ÷ molar mass</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-cyan-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n              <p class=\"font-mono text-lg text-cyan-700\">m = n × M</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">mass = moles × molar mass</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n              <p class=\"font-mono text-lg text-green-700\">M = m/n</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">molar mass = mass ÷ moles</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Moles and Particles -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Moles and Particles\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4 text-center\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <p class=\"font-mono text-lg mb-2\">Number of particles = n × L</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">where L = 6.02 × 10²³</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n              <p class=\"font-mono text-lg mb-2\">n = Particles ÷ L</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">to find moles from particles</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-orange-50 text-left font-semibold text-orange-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-orange-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-orange-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Converting Mass to Particles</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Calculate the number of atoms in 4 g of hydrogen gas (H₂).</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find molar mass of H₂</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-orange-700 mt-1\">M(H₂) = 2 × 1 = 2 g/mol</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate moles of H₂</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">n(H₂) = 4 g ÷ 2 g/mol = 2 mol</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate H₂ molecules</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-teal-700 mt-1\">Molecules = 2 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 1.204 × 10²⁴</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Calculate H atoms</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">Each H₂ molecule has 2 H atoms</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700\">Atoms = 1.204 × 10²⁴ × 2 = 2.408 × 10²⁴ atoms</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Stoichiometry -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Stoichiometry: Reacting Masses\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\"><strong class=\"text-teal-600\">Stoichiometry</strong> is the calculation of quantities of reactants and products in a chemical reaction. The mole ratios from balanced equations allow us to convert between substances.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Steps for Stoichiometric Calculations:</h4>\n            <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li><span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center mr-2 text-xs font-bold\">1</span>Write the balanced chemical equation</li>\n              <li><span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center mr-2 text-xs font-bold\">2</span>Identify the mole ratio from the equation</li>\n              <li><span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center mr-2 text-xs font-bold\">3</span>Convert given quantity to moles</li>\n              <li><span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center mr-2 text-xs font-bold\">4</span>Use mole ratio to find moles of unknown</li>\n              <li><span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center mr-2 text-xs font-bold\">5</span>Convert moles to required quantity</li>\n            </ol>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 1 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -fire mr-2 text-red-500\" data-mi=\"local_fire_department\">local_fire_department</span>Worked Example: Burning Carbon</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Calculate the mass of CO₂ produced when 6 g of carbon burns completely.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Balanced equation</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">C + O₂ → CO₂</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Mole ratio: 1 mol C : 1 mol CO₂</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Moles of C</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">n(C) = 6 ÷ 12 = 0.5 mol</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Moles of CO₂ = 0.5 mol (same ratio)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Mass of CO₂</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">M(CO₂) = 12 + 32 = 44 g/mol</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700\">m(CO₂) = 0.5 × 44 = <strong>22 g</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 2 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -fire-alt mr-2 text-orange-500\" data-mi=\"local_fire_department\">local_fire_department</span>Worked Example: Burning Magnesium</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">What mass of magnesium oxide forms when 12 g of magnesium burns?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Balanced equation</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Mole ratio: 2 mol Mg : 2 mol MgO = 1:1</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Moles of Mg</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">n(Mg) = 12 ÷ 24 = 0.5 mol</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Moles of MgO = 0.5 mol</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Mass of MgO</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-orange-700 mt-1\">M(MgO) = 24 + 16 = 40 g/mol</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-orange-700\">m(MgO) = 0.5 × 40 = <strong>20 g</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Percentage Composition -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n          Percentage Composition\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The percentage composition shows what percentage of the total mass of a compound is contributed by each element.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"font-mono text-lg\">% by mass = (mass of element / Mᵣ of compound) × 100</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Worked Example -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: % Composition of Glucose</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Calculate the % carbon in glucose (C₆H₁₂O₆).</p>\n                \n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find Mᵣ</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">Mᵣ(C₆H₁₂O₆) = (6×12) + (12×1) + (6×16) = 180</p>\n                  </div>\n                  \n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Mass of carbon</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">Mass of C = 6 × 12 = 72</p>\n                  </div>\n                  \n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate %</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">%C = (72/180) × 100 = <strong>40%</strong></p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Empirical & Molecular Formulae -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">7</span>\n          Empirical and Molecular Formulae\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Empirical Formula</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The simplest whole number ratio of atoms.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-orange-600 text-sm mt-2\">Example: CH₂O (for glucose)</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-teal-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-800 mb-2\">Molecular Formula</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The actual number of atoms in a molecule.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-teal-600 text-sm mt-2\">Example: C₆H₁₂O₆ (for glucose)</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-indigo-50 text-left font-semibold text-indigo-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-indigo-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -flask mr-2 text-indigo-500\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Worked Example: Finding Empirical Formula</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">A compound contains 40% C, 6.7% H, and 53.3% O. Find its empirical formula.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n                <table class=\"w-full text-sm mb-3\">\n                  <thead class=\"bg-indigo-100\">\n                    <tr>\n                      <th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Element</th>\n                      <th class=\"p-2\">%</th>\n                      <th class=\"p-2\">÷ Aᵣ</th>\n                      <th class=\"p-2\">Moles</th>\n                      <th class=\"p-2\">÷ smallest</th>\n                      <th class=\"p-2\">Ratio</th>\n                    </tr>\n                  </thead>\n                  <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n                    <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">C</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">40</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">40÷12</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">3.33</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">÷3.33</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-bold\">1</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">H</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">6.7</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">6.7÷1</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">6.7</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">÷3.33</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-bold\">2</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">O</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">53.3</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">53.3÷16</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">3.33</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">÷3.33</td><td class=\"p-2 border font-bold\">1</td></tr>\n                  </tbody>\n                </table>\n              </div>\n              <p class=\"text-green-700 font-bold\">Empirical formula: CH₂O</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Molecular Formula Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-pink-50 text-left font-semibold text-pink-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-pink-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -molecule mr-2 text-pink-500\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Finding Molecular Formula</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">A compound has empirical formula CH₂O and Mᵣ = 180. Find its molecular formula.</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-pink-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Empirical formula mass</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-pink-700 mt-1\">= 12 + (2×1) + 16 = 30</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Find n</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">n = Mᵣ ÷ empirical mass = 180 ÷ 30 = 6</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Multiply empirical formula</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">Molecular formula = (CH₂O)₆ = <strong>C₆H₁₂O₆</strong></p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 8: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-8\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-teal-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. How many moles are in 88 g of CO₂?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>M(CO₂) = 12 + 32 = 44 g/mol</p>\n                <p>n = 88 ÷ 44 = <strong>2 mol</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Calculate the number of molecules in 0.5 mol of water.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Molecules = n × L = 0.5 × 6.02 × 10²³</p>\n                <p>= <strong>3.01 × 10²³ molecules</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. What mass of CaCO₃ contains 0.2 mol?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>M(CaCO₃) = 40 + 12 + 48 = 100 g/mol</p>\n                <p>m = 0.2 × 100 = <strong>20 g</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Fe + Cl₂ → FeCl₃. What mass of FeCl₃ forms from 5.6 g of Fe?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Balanced: 2Fe + 3Cl₂ → 2FeCl₃</p>\n                <p>n(Fe) = 5.6 ÷ 56 = 0.1 mol</p>\n                <p>n(FeCl₃) = 0.1 mol (ratio 1:1)</p>\n                <p>M(FeCl₃) = 56 + 106.5 = 162.5 g/mol</p>\n                <p>m(FeCl₃) = 0.1 × 162.5 = <strong>16.25 g</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-9\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-teal-50 to-cyan-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-teal-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-teal-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Avogadro's number:</strong> L = 6.02 × 10²³ particles/mol</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Mole triangle:</strong> n = m/M, m = n × M, M = m/n</li>\n            <li>• Always use balanced equations for stoichiometry</li>\n            <li>• Mole ratios come from balanced equations</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Empirical formula:</strong> Convert % to moles, find simplest ratio</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Molecular formula:</strong> (Empirical formula)ₙ where n = Mᵣ ÷ empirical mass</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-teal-50 to-cyan-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card {\n      transition: all 0.2s ease;\n    }\n    .step-card:hover {\n      transform: translateX(4px);\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn {\n      transition: all 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover {\n      transform: scale(1.02);\n    }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"mole-concept","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What is Avogadro's number?","options":["6.02 × 10²²","6.02 × 10²³","6.02 × 10²⁴","6.02 × 10²⁵"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Avogadro's number (L) = 6.02 × 10²³ particles per mole."},{"question":"What is the molar mass of H₂O?","options":["16 g/mol","17 g/mol","18 g/mol","20 g/mol"],"correct":2,"explanation":"M(H₂O) = (2×1) + 16 = 18 g/mol"},{"question":"How many moles are in 44 g of CO₂?","options":["0.5 mol","1 mol","2 mol","4 mol"],"correct":1,"explanation":"n = m/M = 44 ÷ 44 = 1 mol"},{"question":"In the equation 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, what is the mole ratio of H₂ to H₂O?","options":["1:1","2:1","1:2","2:2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"From the equation: 2H₂ : 2H₂O = 1:1"},{"question":"What mass of NaCl contains 0.5 mol? (Na=23, Cl=35.5)","options":["29.25 g","58.5 g","11.75 g","23 g"],"correct":0,"explanation":"M(NaCl) = 23 + 35.5 = 58.5 g/mol. m = 0.5 × 58.5 = 29.25 g"},{"question":"A compound has % composition C=40%, H=6.7%, O=53.3%. What is the empirical formula?","options":["CHO","CH₂O","C₂H₂O","C₂H₄O₂"],"correct":1,"explanation":"C: 40/12=3.33, H: 6.7/1=6.7, O: 53.3/16=3.33. Divide by 3.33: C=1, H=2, O=1 → CH₂O"},{"question":"If empirical formula is CH₂ and Mᵣ=28, what is the molecular formula?","options":["CH₂","C₂H₄","C₃H₆","C₄H₈"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Empirical mass = 14. n = 28/14 = 2. Molecular formula = (CH₂)₂ = C₂H₄"},{"question":"Calculate the % carbon in CO₂.","options":["27.3%","33.3%","72.7%","66.7%"],"correct":0,"explanation":"M(CO₂) = 44. Mass of C = 12. %C = (12/44) × 100 = 27.3%"}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"mole-concept","topicTitle":"Mole Concept & Stoichiometry","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8","section-9"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}